===Uruguay vs France===
[[File:Uruguay vs France 2010 World Cup.jpg|thumb|The Uruguayan and French teams warming up]]
France and Uruguay faced each other on 11 June 2010 at the [[Cape Town Stadium]]. Despite a [[Penalty card#Red card|red card]] being given to Uruguay substitute [[Nicolás Lodeiro]] in the second half, Uruguay were able to hold a "lacklustre" France to a 0&ndash;0 draw.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.abc.net.au/news/stories/2010/06/12/2925375.htm |title=French held by Uruguay |date=12 June 2010 |work=[[ABC News (Australia)|ABC News]] |publisher=[[Australian Broadcasting Corporation]] |access-date=29 June 2010 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100614193218/http://www.abc.net.au/news/stories/2010/06/12/2925375.htm |archive-date=14 June 2010 |url-status=dead }}</ref> After the match, former World Cup-winning French player [[Zinedine Zidane]] criticised the French team and particularly coach [[Raymond Domenech]] for a lack of teamwork.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.google.com/hostednews/ap/article/ALeqM5ifRpvLjtAkKommkQLOdGV8morJpgD9GB1S384|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100618092516/http://www.google.com/hostednews/ap/article/ALeqM5ifRpvLjtAkKommkQLOdGV8morJpgD9GB1S384|url-status=dead|archive-date=18 June 2010|title=Zinedine Zidane critical of France team|date=14 June 2010|agency=[[Associated Press]]|access-date=29 June 2010}}</ref> Domenech claimed after the match to be "happy with the overall performance".<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.abc.net.au/news/stories/2010/06/12/2925489.htm?site=sport&section=all|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121111081557/http://www.abc.net.au/news/stories/2010/06/12/2925489.htm?site=sport&section=all|url-status=dead|archive-date=11 November 2012|title=France frustrated by stalemate|date=12 June 2010|work=[[ABC News (Australia)|ABC News]]|publisher=[[Australian Broadcasting Corporation]]|access-date=29 June 2010}}</ref>

