===South Africa vs Uruguay===
Uruguay took the lead in the 24th minute, when [[Diego Forlán]] launched a shot from 30 yards out that beat goalkeeper [[Itumeleng Khune]], who did not attempt to save the shot.<ref name="fifa.com">{{cite web |url=http://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2010/m=6/news=forlan-silences-south-africa-1246686.html |title=Forlan silences South Africa |website=FIFA.com |access-date=15 January 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160407211508/http://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2010/m=6/news=forlan-silences-south-africa-1246686.html |archive-date=7 April 2016 |url-status=dead}}</ref> In the second half, [[Luis Suárez]] was left through on goal, but he was brought down by Khune. Referee [[Massimo Busacca]] awarded a penalty and showed Khune a red card.<ref name="fifa.com"/> Deep into injury time, Uruguay scored their third goal when [[Álvaro Pereira]] tapped in a Suárez cross.<ref name="fifa.com"/> This was Uruguay's first World Cup win since 1990.

